description: Thursday Arena bot — canonical rules and architecture
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root before changing anything. It is the canonical handbook:
architecture, hard rules, commands, invariants, how to verify a change, and where the evidence lives.

The five that bite hardest:

1. Never point a browser at `~/.config/google-chrome`. `lib/cdp.js` refuses it — Playwright's
   `--use-mock-keychain` made Chrome wipe the user's cookies once already, unrecoverably. Use the
   dedicated profile (`ARENA_PROFILE`).
2. `npm test`, `npm run eval`, `tools/eval_matches.js`, `tools/merge_book.js`, and
   `npm run book:build` use local data. `play:dry` reads the live account without an arena POST;
   `rank` is live and read-only. Play and climb spend rating; MCP's `arena_act` can mutate.
3. Never reintroduce heuristics — archetype labels, name ban/prefer lists, "recipes", threat
   formulas. All were measured worse than the simulator and deleted. `lib/sim.js` is ground truth and
   must keep matching all 10,748 recorded winners and the recorded frame checks.
4. Don't edit code while rated games are running. Stop the loop, change, test, restart.
5. A planner change ships only if `tools/eval_matches.js` beats the baseline on both seasons.

`lib/planner.js` is the only module that decides anything. `driver/play_loop.js` turns its output
into server actions safely and holds no strategy.
